menu "Night Sentinel network"

    config NS_WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi SSID (optional fallback)"
        default ""
        help
            Network to try when nothing has been saved from the setup page yet.
            Leave empty to always start in setup mode on first boot.
            The board can't see 5 GHz networks.

    config NS_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Wi-Fi password (optional fallback)"
        default ""
        help
            Stored in sdkconfig, which is git-ignored, so it never reaches GitHub.

    config NS_PORTAL_SSID
        string "Setup hotspot name"
        default "NightSentinel-Setup"
        help
            Hotspot the board opens when it can't join a network. Join it from a phone and
            open http://192.168.4.1/ to pick a nearby network and type its password.

    config NS_PORTAL_PASSWORD
        string "Setup hotspot password"
        default "sentinel123"
        help
            8+ characters for WPA2. Shorter (or empty) makes the hotspot open, so anyone
            nearby could see the home password you type into the page.

    config NS_NTFY_SERVER
        string "ntfy server"
        default "https://ntfy.sh"
        help
            Phone push service. Install the ntfy app and subscribe to the topic below.

    config NS_NTFY_TOPIC
        string "ntfy topic (keep it secret)"
        default ""
        help
            Anyone who knows the topic can read the alerts and photos, so use 20+ random
            characters, e.g. ns-7f3kq9w2... It lives in sdkconfig, which is git-ignored.
            Empty = no phone push (events are still spoken and saved to SD).

    config NS_TZ
        string "Time zone (POSIX TZ string)"
        default "IST-5:30"
        help
            Used for event file names and timestamps. India: IST-5:30.
            Central Europe: CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3.

endmenu
